# dsh-discord-bot — supplying the token through the environment.
#
# This is the third of three sources, after the plugin row's `token` and
# `tokenFile`. Use it when dsh is started by something that already manages
# secrets (a launchd plist, a systemd unit, a container runtime); prefer
# `tokenFile` for an ordinary desktop install, since a shell environment is
# easier to leak into a process listing than a mode-600 file.
#
# Either name is accepted; DSH_DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN wins when both are set.

DSH_DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=
